note draft
# Checked spec, not compiled code: `mine`/`form`/`any`/`range`/`send` are the feed grammar DSL's own vocabulary
# (note/term/feed/01-grammar.md), never real Term identifiers, so this file can never pass `term make`'s type
# checker and is shelved from the build on purpose, the same as every mine.tree/mint.tree in this package and in
# @term/mill. The real, compiling reader for this dialect is ./code.tree. See note/term/feed/05-parser-and-mill.md.
#
# `send <name>` emits a match as a named field on the enclosing rule. `take`/`bind` is reserved for parameters a
# rule receives from its caller (mine int's width/order/sign, an offset passed down for mine at) — hex needs none.

mine hex
  mine list
    mine form, form hex-byte

mine hex-byte
  mine form, form hex-digit
    send high
  mine form, form hex-digit
    send low

mine hex-digit
  mine any
    mine range
      bind base, text <0>
      bind head, text <9>
    mine range
      bind base, text <a>
      bind head, text <f>
    mine range
      bind base, text <A>
      bind head, text <F>
